==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|curiusly}}, {{m|enm|curyously}}, {{m|enm|curiosly}}, {{m|enm|curiouseliche}}, {{m|enm|curyouslyche}}, equivalent to {{af|en|curious|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkjɝi.əsli/|/ˈkjʊɹi.əsli/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkjʊəɹi.əsli/|/ˈkjɔːɹi.əsli/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-curiously.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyph|en|cu|ri|ous|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[curious]] manner; with curiosity; [[inquisitive]]ly.
#: {{ux|en|The children peeped '''curiously''' into the attic room.}}
# {{U|oddly}}; in a strange or unexpected way.
#: {{ux|en|'''Curiously''', when I arrived home, the front door was standing ajar.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|date=1988-10-07|author=Laura Molzahn|title=Between Heaven and the Gargabe Can|work=w:Chicago Reader|url=http://www.chicagoreader.com/chicago/between-heaven-and-the-gargabe-can/Content?oid=872846|passage=Performing a '''curiously''' melancholy, undulating developpe, the dancers point their legs at each other like accusing fingers.|accessdate=3 January 2025|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160306200506/http://www.chicagoreader.com/chicago/between-heaven-and-the-gargabe-can/Content?oid=872846|archivedate=6 March 2016}}

